    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0496" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3234: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sammons</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-02T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 2,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            October 2, 10.30 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Tong Shao-yi, Chief of Southern Peace Delegation, disgusted with both Northern
                    and Southern military party tactics, sent official seal and resignation to
                        latter.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d346-f1"/> Legation notified.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sammons</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d346-f1" n="59" xml:id="d346-f1-content">
                <p>For report of the refusal to accept his resignation, see <ref target="#pg396">p.
                        396</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
